1019      +  GLOBAL MACRO USAGE: calling %tmtoevnt/%m_tmtoevnt directly was not used (both always produce
1020      +  three separate output files with their own tnf.inc titlekeys that don't exist - only the bare
1021      +  "t-os" key is defined - conflicting with the single-PDF-per-titlekey requirement). Per-macro
1022      +  priority, the relevant CODE was instead pulled directly from tmtoevnt.sas's internal %cumrate
1023      +  and %hratio submacros and adapted below rather than written from scratch:
1024      +     - TIME statement convention: tmtoevnt.sas's %hratio submacro uses
1025      +       `model &dvar*&cvar(0) = &colvar` - adapted here as `aval*cnsr(1)` (ADTTE.CNSR follows the
1026      +       standard ADaM direction: 0=event, 1=censored, so CNSR itself is used directly with no
1027      +       derived indicator variable needed).
1028      +     - Hazard ratio: tmtoevnt.sas's %hratio submacro uses `class &colvar(ref=...)/param=ref;
1029      +       model .../rl; hazardratio &colvar / diff=ref;` - the `/rl` model option is what actually
1030      +       populates HRLowerCL/HRUpperCL in the ParameterEstimates ODS table (a prior revision of
1031      +       this program omitted /rl, which would have left the hazard ratio CI blank).
                                                                    The SAS System

1032      +     - Median OS and landmark survival rate: tmtoevnt.sas's %cumrate submacro drives
1033      +       `strata &colvar;` off the PROC LIFETEST TIME statement and captures ODS Quartiles /
1034      +       ProductLimitEstimates output data sets - the same ODS tables (Quartiles,
1035      +       ProductLimitEstimates, HomTests, ParameterEstimates) are used below.
1036      +     - Rendering: %tabdesc/%tabcount build the standard COMBINE dataset (linlabel/sortord/
1037      +       statord/value1-value&_maxcol/level) for the Events/Censored/Duration count rows, exactly
1038      +       as t-disp.sas/t-aebrief.sas do; the KM median/KM rate/Hazard Ratio/log-rank rows are built
1039      +       directly in that SAME field structure and appended into COMBINE via a plain `data
1040      +       combine; set combine ...;` step (mirroring the production reference program
1041      +       G:\projects\p627\s21\ia01\version1\prog\t-os-a.sas, which does
1042      +       `set combine t odd pval;`) - %tabprep/%printset/%tabdrpt then render the whole table in
1043      +       one pass, keeping the font/page layout identical across all 5 tables. A prior revision of
1044      +       this program built a separate hand-rolled PROC REPORT dataset instead, which is why the
1045      +       KM estimate rows were not appearing in the rendered PDF.
1046      +     - Blank separator rows: appended at the END of each section (same sortord as that section's
1047      +       last row, statord='9' so it sorts last) - TABPREP
1048      +       (`if first.sortord and linlabel=' ' then delete;`) only deletes a blank-linlabel row when
1049      +       it is the FIRST record of its sortord group, so a trailing blank row survives.
1050      +     - Duration of OS follow-up: not directly produced by tmtoevnt.sas; implemented per the
1051      +       shell's explicit ">= 6/12/18 Months" categories (label wording confirmed against the
1052      +       production reference program's dur1t-dur5t formats) as a PROC SQL count of participants
1053      +       with AVAL (analysis time to event or censoring) at least that long - the minimum
1054      +       demonstrated follow-up, not a KM/reverse-KM estimate. Built as a SQL count (not TABCOUNT)
1055      +       so a row always appears, even "0 (0.0%)", when no participant reaches a given threshold.
1056      +
1057      +  ASSUMPTION (confirmed 20260830 - ADSL/ADTTE were updated so AVAL is in DAYS, matching this):
1058      +  ADTTE is assumed to follow standard CDISC ADaM BDS time-to-event conventions:
1059      +     AVAL   = analysis time in DAYS from randomization/first dose to event or censoring
